  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to raising the maximum\nfine for persons who violate the law regulating telemarketing",
    "basePrintNo": "S4617",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4617-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §399-z, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4617\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to raising the\nmaximum fine for persons who violate the law regulating telemarketing\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to deter any would-be violators of the Do\nNot Call Registry.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the general business law by increasing the fine applied\nto violators of the Do Not Call Registry to $20,000.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Do Not Call Registry has been an effective tool in curbing the\nnumber of unwanted calls most households receive from companies wishing\nto solicit information or business. However, there are a number of\nactors who are violating this law in the hopes of gaining business from\nunwitting participants. This is a calculated decision that they are\nmaking as a part of their overall business model. Their calculus is that\nthey will earn more business by violating the law than they will lose in\nfines from people reporting their misdeeds.  This bill aims to further\ncurb these entities from violating the Do Not Call Registry by increas-\ning the fine per violation by almost double, thereby encouraging further\ncompliance with the law.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22 - S. 4585 - Consumer Protection Committee/A. 83 - Passed Assem-\nbly.\n\n2019-20 - S. 4515 - Consumer Protection Committee.\n\n2017-18 - S. 3152 - Rules Committee/A. 3734 - Consumer Affairs Commit-\ntee.\n\n2016 - S. 6553 Rules Committee/A. 9442 - Consumer Affairs Committee.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
